WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.990
- [Narrator] Walk into any Waffle House

00:00:01.990 --> 00:00:04.670
and you'll be greeted by the
familiar sounds of breakfast:

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:07.530
Bacon sizzling, coffee
brewing, hash browns crunching,

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:08.680
and the piercing ding

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:10.760
of a waffle iron ready for more batter.

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:14.232
But listen closely and you'll
hear a truly unique sound.

00:00:14.232 --> 00:00:17.526
♪ There are raisins in my toast ♪

00:00:17.526 --> 00:00:18.359
- [Narrator] What's that?

00:00:18.359 --> 00:00:19.730
"There are Raisins in My Toast."

00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:21.976
Who writes a song about toast?

00:00:21.976 --> 00:00:25.752
♪ There are raisins in my toast ♪

00:00:25.752 --> 00:00:28.662
♪ Raisin toast at Waffle House ♪

00:00:28.662 --> 00:00:31.680
- [Narrator] Ladies and
gentlemen, meet Shelby.

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:34.900
- I'm Shelby White, and I'm the
President of Waffle Records.

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:36.248
- [Narrator] Waffle what?

00:00:36.248 --> 00:00:39.450
- Waffle Records is the
in-house record label

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:40.570
of Waffle House.

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:41.782
- [Narrator] Waffle Records?

00:00:41.782 --> 00:00:42.615
Of course.

00:00:42.615 --> 00:00:44.250
- [Shelby] Waffle Records
was created as a way

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:46.960
to add waffle content to the jukebox.

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:50.180
We originally created the songs in 1984.

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:51.440
Chairman said, you know what?

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:52.853
We need a record label.

00:00:53.936 --> 00:00:58.700
There are currently 47 Waffle
House songs on the jukebox.

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:00.340
Some of our songs on the jukebox are

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:02.650
"Special Lady at the Waffle House."

00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:04.538
♪ Special lady ♪

00:01:04.538 --> 00:01:05.690
- [Shelby] "Grill Operator."

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:07.870
♪ I'm a grill operator ♪

00:01:07.870 --> 00:01:10.372
- [Shelby] "I Saw Elvis
at the Waffle House."

00:01:10.372 --> 00:01:13.860
♪ Last night I saw Elvis
at the Waffle House ♪

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:14.850
- [Narrator] Building a record label

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:17.160
all about breakfast
foods is no small feat.

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:19.250
So Shelby and the team
at Waffle House turned

00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:22.053
to music producers like Jason Phelps.

00:01:22.053 --> 00:01:23.920
- Hi, I'm Jason Phelps.

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:26.530
I write and produce
music for Waffle Records.

00:01:26.530 --> 00:01:27.970
To make a song for Waffle House,

00:01:27.970 --> 00:01:29.940
it starts with an idea.

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:32.341
And that idea, generally, is the title

00:01:32.341 --> 00:01:34.890
or what the song's going to be about.

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:35.820
- [Narrator] Sometimes the idea

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:38.540
is more serious like
veterans returning home.

00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:40.510
But, sometimes it's more silly

00:01:40.510 --> 00:01:42.310
like having raisins in your toast.

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:44.840
- This last song that we did called 

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:46.950
"Only at the Waffle House" was
very much about crazy things

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:48.693
that can happen at the Waffle House.

00:01:48.693 --> 00:01:53.026
♪ Only at the Waffle House ♪

00:01:53.026 --> 00:01:57.525
♪ That yellow light shining down ♪

00:01:57.525 --> 00:02:00.160
♪ It's where I break from the long road ♪

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:01.393
People give birth at the Waffle House.

00:02:01.393 --> 00:02:05.070
Somebody one time rode a
horse to the Waffle House.

00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:06.270
There are lots of things that happen;

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:09.860
so the songs almost end up
sort of writing themselves

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:12.131
once you have all this good content.

00:02:12.131 --> 00:02:15.450
We do take it very seriously
in terms of our craft,

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:18.720
but music is fun and
the Waffle House is fun.

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:20.261
Who doesn't like that marriage?

00:02:20.261 --> 00:02:24.261
♪ Yeah, only at the Waffle House ♪

